      "params_json": "{\"actions\":[\"new_product\",\"new_variant\"],\"reference\":\"owner-confirmed canonical registry nodes and explicit aliases\",\"compare_against\":\"original listing evidence, independently of predicted labels\",\"match_level\":\"entity being created\",\"require_positive_identity_match\":true,\"resolve_model_variant_boundaries\":true,\"ignore\":[\"capitalization\",\"optional family levels\",\"package quantity\"],\"infer_aliases_from_label_mismatch\":false,\"missing_brand_field_triggers\":false}",
      "rationale": "Reuses twin_of for duplicate creation caused by canonical naming or model–variant boundary differences. Independent source-to-registry matching avoids an echo check; exact-label disagreement alone cannot trigger it. It could unnecessarily defer legitimate close line extensions when discriminating evidence is missing, so abstain rather than veto. It cannot recover unsupported variants or establish unrecorded synonyms. These inspected cases motivate the rule; they do not establish holdout performance."
